# tools/al/ales_stereo_soft_center_clip_witness.rish -- stereo_soft_center_clip: the soft center clipper carried into stereo with ONE SHARED CONTINUOUS DEAD ZONE, both channels in lockstep, the phase-holding yet
# ratio-breaking member of the stereo dead-zone corner (ALES142).
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus - the creative suite) - waymark ALES - rung ALES142.
# Design read: active-designing/date/20260815/20260815-042641_fill-ales142-lotus-stereo-soft-center-clip.md
# Stands on: lotus/soft_center_clip.rye (ALES88 -- the mono soft center clipper run once per channel, y = if |x| ≤ t then 0 else x − sign(x)-t with no rail edge), lotus/stereo_center_clip.rye (ALES141 -- the hard
# sibling whose dead zone this shares and whose survivors this pulls toward zero by t, the soft/hard bond), lotus/pan.rye (ALES10 -- the StereoClip, two mono Clips left/right, and its balance invariant),
# lotus/timeline.rye (ALES2 -- the Clip, its buf/len/samples, sample_min/max). A Lotus master is a StereoClip whose defining invariant is that left and right hold the same length. This rung carries ALES88's continuous
# dead zone into stereo -- silencing the quiet middle and shifting every survivor toward zero by the threshold in both channels, the survivor rising continuously from zero, one dead zone landing on both speakers
# together. The soft center clip is the continuous twin of ALES141's hard center clip, which jumped at the boundary. It is odd, so it holds the inter-channel antisymmetry (an out-of-phase master staying out of phase),
# yet it is a shift, so it breaks the inter-channel ratio (a one-to-two master not staying one-to-two) and is not idempotent -- the honest middle of the class.
#
# lotus/stereo_soft_center_clip.rye validates both channels once against the shared threshold and length before either is mutated (BadThreshold on a threshold outside [0, sample_max], BadRange on a span outside the
# samples), then soft-center-clips both channels through ALES88's soft_center_clip; SoftCenterClipError reused whole. The crux is four laws. THE STEREO SOFT CENTER-CLIP LAW: each channel equals ALES88's mono
# soft_center_clip with the same threshold byte for byte. THE BALANCE / LENGTH LAW: left.len == right.len after, both holding their starting length. THE PER-CHANNEL ODD / SHIFT LAW: the antisymmetry held, the ratio
# broken, the map not idempotent, an identical-channel master staying identical, thresh 0 the identity, the soft/hard bond soft magnitude equals hard magnitude minus t on every survivor against ALES141. THE ATOMICITY
# / DEGENERATE LAW: a refusal leaves both channels untouched and balanced, thresh 0 the identity, count 0 the identity.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/al/ales_stereo_soft_center_clip_witness.rish

say "ales-stereo-soft-center-clip: Language EN — stereo_soft_center_clip soft-center-clips a span in both channels of a stereo master with the same threshold, silencing every sample whose magnitude is at most the threshold and shifting every louder sample toward zero by exactly the threshold, the same continuous dead zone on each, so one soft center clip lands on both speakers together. A Lotus master is two Clips heard together, one per speaker, whose defining invariant is that left and right hold the same length so the two channels stay aligned in time. This rung carries the continuous twin of ALES141's hard center clip on ALES88's soft center clipper, running the proven mono soft center clip on each channel with the same threshold, validated once against the shared threshold and length before either channel is mutated so a refusal never soft-center-clips one channel and leaves the other whole."
say "ales-stereo-soft-center-clip: Style Radiant — where ALES141's hard center clip passes the loud unchanged and leaves a jump at the boundary, the soft center clip silences the same quiet middle and then shifts every survivor toward zero by exactly the threshold, so the survivor rises continuously from zero rather than leaping, the floor-side twin of ALES133's soft drive on the ceiling. The soft center clip is odd, because the shift of the sign times the threshold flips with the sign, so like the hard center clip it holds the inter-channel antisymmetry: an out-of-phase master, right the exact negation of left, comes back still out of phase, right still the negation of left. Yet unlike the hard center clip it is a shift, not a mask, and a shift is not scale-invariant, so the soft form breaks the inter-channel ratio: a one-to-two master does not stay one-to-two, because subtracting the same threshold from both channels' survivors pulls the quieter one proportionally harder, two x minus t not equal to two times x minus t. And it is not idempotent, because each pass subtracts the threshold again. This is the honest middle of the class, stated plainly rather than dressed in a symmetry it lacks: the hard center clip held both ratio and antisymmetry and was idempotent, the soft center clip holds only the antisymmetry. What both dead-zone members share, carried into stereo, is the same dead zone and the soft-hard bond: on every survivor the soft magnitude equals the hard magnitude minus the threshold, per channel, proven against ALES141. The rule is stated positively: the soft center clip is exact for every i16 with no rail edge and no saturate, a positive survivor landing in one through sample_max, a negative in sample_min through minus one, the dead zone at zero; it carries one parameter, the threshold magnitude, and names two faults. Refuse BadThreshold on a threshold outside zero through sample_max and BadRange on a span outside the samples, each before either channel is mutated, else soft-center-clip both channels over the span with the same threshold via ALES88's soft center clip. It reuses ALES88's SoftCenterClipError by name and ALES88's soft center clip for the arithmetic, inventing no new fault and no new primitive. The crux stands out as four laws: the stereo soft center-clip law, the balance / length law, the per-channel odd / shift law (the antisymmetry held, the ratio broken, the map not idempotent, an identical-channel master staying identical, threshold zero the identity, the soft-hard bond per survivor), and the atomicity / degenerate law (any refusal leaves both channels byte for byte untouched and still balanced, threshold zero the identity on both, count zero the identity on both)."
say "ales-stereo-soft-center-clip: Lens TAME — two bounded i16 Clips (left, right) soft-center-clipped in lockstep by one shared continuous dead zone; the balance invariant is asserted on entry and exit, the threshold and span are bound-checked once before any write, and because those checks hold identically for both channels each mono soft center clip is pre-validated to succeed so no refusal can land between the two channel edits; soft_center_clip walks the span once per channel, taking each magnitude in i32 so the magnitude of sample_min is representable and shifting each survivor toward zero by the threshold with its sign held, the output landing in the i16 rail by construction so there is no rail edge and no saturate, never touching a byte past len so the length holds exactly; it reuses ALES88's soft center clip per channel over its public API and ALES88's SoftCenterClipError whole, inventing no new primitive; the stereo soft center-clip law is proven against ALES88's own soft center clip run per channel, the per-channel odd / shift law proves the out-of-phase field's antisymmetry is held while the one-to-two field's ratio breaks and the map is not idempotent, and the soft-hard bond is proven against ALES141's stereo center clip, the two refusals leave both channels byte-for-byte untouched, and threshold zero is the identity; siloed to lotus/, no real sample rate, no network, no keys, no funds, no device, no speaker."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "lotus/bin/stereo_soft_center_clip"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p lotus/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/stereo_soft_center_clip.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "ales-stereo-soft-center-clip: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "lotus/bin/stereo_soft_center_clip.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "ales-stereo-soft-center-clip: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "ales-stereo-soft-center-clip: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN ales-stereo-soft-center-clip' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "ales-stereo-soft-center-clip: selftest did not print the GREEN ales-stereo-soft-center-clip line"
